{"book":23,"chapter":39,"context":{"chapter":39,"title":"Envoys From Babylon","summary":"Envoys from Merodach-baladan of Babylon visit Hezekiah, who shows them all his treasures. Isaiah announces that everything, and some of Hezekiah's descendants, will one day be carried to Babylon, but Hezekiah is relieved there will be peace in his own days.","background":"Merodach-baladan was a Chaldean leader who twice seized Babylon's throne and repeatedly rebelled against Assyria; his name appears in Assyrian and Babylonian records. His envoys likely hoped to recruit Judah into a revolt. The chapter is the book's hinge, pointing to the Babylonian exile that chapters 40–66 address.","customs":[{"term":"Eunuchs in the palace","verses":"39:7","note":"Young royals from conquered lands were often taken to serve at a foreign court. Daniel and his friends were taken to Babylon's palace (Daniel 1:3-4)."}],"watchFor":["'There is nothing among my treasures that I have not shewed them' (v. 4).","Hezekiah's reply looks only to his own lifetime (v. 8)."],"connections":["2 Kings 20:12-19","2 Chronicles 32:31","Daniel 1:3-4","2 Kings 24:13"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["בָּעֵת","ba'et","H6256","HRd/Ncbsa","at the time"],["הַהִוא","hahiv'","H1931","HTd/Pp3fs","<the> that"],["שָׁלַח","shalach","H7971","HVqp3ms","he sent"],["מְרֹדַךְ","merodakh","H4757","HNpm","Merodach-"],["בַּלְאֲדָן","bal'adon","H4757","HNpm","Baladan"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["בַּלְאֲדָן","bal'adan","H1081","HNpm","Baladan"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh-","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["בָּבֶל","bavel","H894","HNpl","Babylon"],["סְפָרִים","sefarim","H5612","HNcmpa","letters"],["וּמִנְחָה","uminchah","H4503","HC/Ncfsa","and a gift"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["חִזְקִיָּהוּ","chizkiyahu","H2396","HNpm","Hezekiah"],["וַיִּשְׁמַע","vaiyishma'","H8085","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he had heard"],["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","that"],["חָלָה","chalah","H2470","HVqp3ms","he had been sick"],["וַיֶּחֱזָק","vaiyechezak","H2388","